    {
      "title": "Make it your own",
      "slug": "make-it-your-own",
      "displayOrder": 51,
      "legacy": {
        "itemId": 177,
        "lessonOrder": 51
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "Are your sweaters too short in front?  Do you find that you are always tugging them down?<br>\r\nBust darts are the answer ... yes ... even in knits!<br>\r\nAdd additional length to the center front .... no more tugging!<br>\r\n<div class=\"lecture-attachment\">\r\n<img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/27/summer_tee/seraina5a.jpg\"><br>Even our model, Esmeralda could use a bit of extra length in the front.  Notice how the front hem isn't straight and there is a slight wrinkle from side seam to bust point.\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/27/summer_tee/bust-darts1.png\">\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 2212,
